#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:3
msgid "Troubleshoot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:5
msgid ""
"Diagnose and fix common pipx problems, from wrong package versions to broken "
"environments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:9
msgid "Wrong package version installed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:11
msgid ""
"pipx builds venvs with your default Python, and pip installs the newest "
"release compatible with it. When a package drops support for your Python "
"version, pip installs an older release without warning."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:14
msgid "Check which Python pipx uses:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:16
msgid "$ pipx environment --value PIPX_DEFAULT_PYTHON"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:20
msgid "Install with a different Python:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:22
msgid "$ pipx install my-package --python python3.12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:26
msgid ""
"If the package is already installed, reinstall it instead; ``pipx install --"
"force`` ignores ``--python``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:28
msgid "$ pipx reinstall my-package --python python3.12"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:32
msgid "If you do not have that version, let pipx download a standalone build:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:34
msgid "$ pipx install my-package --python 3.13 --fetch-python=missing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:38
msgid ""
"Pass ``--fetch-python=always`` to download even when the system has the "
"requested version, for example to avoid a patched distro interpreter. See :"
"doc:`standalone-python`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:45
msgid "Diagnose and repair environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:47
msgid "Check each managed environment without changing it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:49 ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:301
msgid "$ pipx health"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:53
msgid ""
"The command exits with status 1 when an environment cannot run its Python "
"interpreter. Pass package names to check a subset, or ``--output json`` to "
"read the result from a script; each unhealthy environment then appears in "
"``errors`` with the code ``environment_unhealthy``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:57
msgid "Repair failed environments with the default Python:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:59
msgid "$ pipx repair"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:63
msgid ""
"Pass package names to limit the repair, and ``--python`` when the rebuilt "
"environments need another interpreter:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:65
msgid "$ pipx repair --python python3.13"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:69
msgid ""
"``pipx repair`` reuses the recorded metadata, like ``pipx reinstall``, and "
"leaves healthy environments unchanged. It refuses a pinned package because "
"its recorded source may resolve to another release; run ``pipx unpin "
"PACKAGE`` first. To rebuild healthy environments too (for example after an "
"old pipx release), use ``pipx reinstall-all`` (see :doc:`manage-installed-"
"apps`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:76
msgid ""
"A package installed with a pipx before 0.15.0.0 has no recorded options. To "
"specify options, uninstall and install it manually:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:79
msgid ""
"$ pipx uninstall <mypackage>\n"
"$ pipx install <mypackage>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:86
msgid "Start over from a fresh install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:88
msgid ""
"An interrupted install or shared-library upgrade can leave state that ``pipx "
"repair`` cannot mend. Reset pipx to the state it had at install time:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:91
msgid "$ pipx reset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:95
msgid ""
"It uninstalls every managed package (unlinking their apps and man pages) and "
"removes the shared libraries, caches, standalone interpreters, logs, and "
"trash. Because it asks first, ``--yes`` answers for a script, and ``--dry-"
"run`` lists what it would remove without touching anything:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:99
msgid "$ pipx reset --dry-run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:103
msgid ""
"Record what you have with ``pipx list --short`` before the reset, then "
"reinstall afterward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:107
msgid "Specify options that take an argument"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:109
msgid "Use an ``=`` sign for options that require an argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:111
msgid "$ pipx install pycowsay --pip-args=\"--no-cache-dir\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:115
msgid "To ignore SSL/TLS errors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:117
msgid ""
"$ pipx install termpair --pip-args '--trusted-host files.pythonhosted.org --"
"trusted-host pypi.org --trusted-host pypi.python.org --trusted-host github."
"com'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:123
msgid "Check for PIP_* environment variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:125
msgid ""
"Under the pip backend, ``PIP_*`` environment variables change how pipx "
"installs and upgrades packages. If pipx behaves strangely on install or "
"upgrade, check for them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:128 ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:269
msgid "Unix or macOS:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:130
msgid "$ env | grep '^PIP_'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:134
msgid "Windows PowerShell:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:136
msgid "$ ls env:PIP_*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:140
msgid "Windows ``cmd``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:142
msgid "$ set PIP_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:146
msgid ""
"See `pip's environment variables <https://pip.pypa.io/en/stable/user_guide/"
"#environment-variables>`_. The uv backend ignores ``PIP_*`` and reads uv's "
"own ``UV_*`` variables (for example ``UV_INDEX_URL``) instead; check for "
"those the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:152
msgid "Clear runpip cache warnings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:154
msgid ""
"Under the pip backend, ``pipx runpip`` runs pip from pipx's shared libraries "
"with a pipx-managed venv's interpreter. Warnings such as ``WARNING: Cache "
"entry deserialization failed, entry ignored`` come from that pip and its own "
"HTTP cache, not from pipx's venv cache."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:158
msgid "Inspect and clear the cache for a managed package:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:160
msgid ""
"$ pipx runpip <package> cache dir\n"
"$ pipx runpip <package> cache purge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:165
msgid ""
"Clearing pipx's venv cache (``pipx environment --value PIPX_VENV_CACHEDIR``) "
"or the cache for a different interpreter does not clear entries used by "
"``pipx runpip <package>``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:168
msgid ""
"Under the uv backend, ``pipx runpip`` runs ``uv pip``, which has no "
"``cache`` subcommand. Use uv's cache commands with the binary pipx uses "
"(``pipx environment --value PIPX_UV_BINARY``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:171
msgid ""
"$ uv cache dir\n"
"$ uv cache clean"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:178
msgid "Log files"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:180
msgid ""
"pipx writes a verbose log for every command to ``pipx environment --value "
"PIPX_LOG_DIR``. By default that is ``~/.local/state/pipx/log`` on Linux "
"(``$XDG_STATE_HOME/pipx/log``), ``~/Library/Logs/pipx`` on macOS, and "
"``%LOCALAPPDATA%\\pipx\\pipx\\Logs`` on Windows, or ``$PIPX_HOME/logs`` when "
"``PIPX_HOME`` is set. When that directory is not writable, pipx falls back "
"to the platform user log directory. A command that fails while pip or uv "
"runs also writes the backend output beside its log, as "
"``cmd_<timestamp>_pip_errors.log`` or ``cmd_<timestamp>_uv_errors.log``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:186
msgid ""
"pipx keeps the logs of the last 10 commands, counting the one that is "
"running, and separately the last 10 error logs. Set ``PIPX_MAX_LOGS`` to "
"change both limits. ``0`` acts like ``1``: the latest command's log stays, "
"because a failing command points you at its error log. pipx never deletes "
"the logs of a command that is still running in another pipx process, so "
"concurrent commands can briefly leave more logs than the limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:193
msgid "Lazy imports on Python 3.15"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:195
msgid ""
"On Python 3.15 pipx makes every import in its process lazy (:pep:`810`) to "
"start faster. A missing or broken dependency then fails where pipx first "
"uses it, with ``lazy import of 'X' raised an exception during resolution``, "
"instead of at startup. To load modules eagerly, set "
"``PYTHON_LAZY_IMPORTS=normal`` or run ``python -X lazy_imports=normal -m "
"pipx``; pipx keeps a mode you set either way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:204
msgid "``sudo pipx`` not found"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:206
msgid ""
"If you installed pipx with ``pip install --user``, its binary lives in your "
"user directory (for example ``~/.local/bin/pipx``). Root's ``PATH`` does not "
"include that directory, so ``sudo pipx`` fails with \"command not found\". "
"Use the full path:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:210
msgid "$ sudo ~/.local/bin/pipx ensurepath --global"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:214
msgid ""
"To avoid this, install pipx through your distribution's package manager "
"(``apt install pipx``, ``dnf install pipx``) or system-wide with ``sudo pip "
"install pipx`` (without ``--user``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:219
msgid "A suffixed app runs under a new name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:221
msgid ""
"pipx 1.17.14 and earlier put ``--suffix`` before the last dot of an app "
"name, so ``pipx install pip --suffix=_old`` exposed ``pip3_old.12``. Later "
"releases put it at the end, ``pip3.12_old``; on Windows it still goes before "
"a file extension such as ``.exe`` or ``.py``, so the file keeps opening. "
"After you upgrade pipx, an app keeps its old name and ``pipx list`` shows it "
"under that name. The next ``pipx upgrade``, ``reinstall``, ``inject``, or "
"``expose`` of the environment renames it and logs ``Renamed pip3_old.12 to "
"pip3.12_old``. Update scripts and aliases that call the old name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:230
msgid "``Cannot create ...: permission denied``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:232
msgid ""
"pipx creates its home, binary, and manual page directories before any "
"command that may write to them. When the current user cannot create one, "
"pipx exits with this error and names the directory. With ``--global`` the "
"defaults sit under ``/opt/pipx`` and ``/usr/local``, so run the command with "
"``sudo``. Otherwise, or to keep the installation out of system directories, "
"point ``PIPX_HOME``, ``PIPX_BIN_DIR``, and ``PIPX_MAN_DIR`` (or their "
"``PIPX_GLOBAL_*`` counterparts) at directories you can write; see :doc:"
"`configure-paths`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:240
msgid "Debian and Ubuntu issues"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:242
msgid ""
"On Debian, Ubuntu, and derivatives, make sure these packages are installed; "
"Debian systems do not add them by default:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:244
msgid "$ sudo apt install python3-venv python3-pip"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:248
msgid ""
"See the `Python Packaging User Guide <https://packaging.python.org/guides/"
"installing-using-linux-tools>`_ on installing pip, setuptools, and wheel "
"with Linux package managers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:254
msgid "Naming a pipx app in your own shebang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:256
msgid ""
"The default pipx home on macOS is ``~/Library/Application Support/pipx``, "
"which contains a space. Apps installed there run because pip and uv write a "
"``/bin/sh`` wrapper as the shebang whenever the interpreter path holds a "
"space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:259
msgid ""
"A shebang you write yourself has no such wrapper. ``#!/Users/you/.local/bin/"
"aws`` works, while a shebang naming a path with a space does not, because "
"the kernel reads the first space as the end of the interpreter path. Point "
"your shebang at ``PIPX_BIN_DIR`` (``~/.local/bin`` by default, no space), or "
"set ``PIPX_HOME`` to a path without spaces."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:265
msgid "Does it install with plain pip?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:267
msgid ""
"To tell whether pipx or the package is at fault, try installing the package "
"with pip."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:271
msgid ""
"$ python3 -m venv test_venv\n"
"$ test_venv/bin/python3 -m pip install <problem-package>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:276
msgid "Windows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:278
msgid ""
"$ python -m venv test_venv\n"
"$ test_venv/Scripts/python -m pip install <problem-package>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:283
msgid ""
"If pip also fails, the problem is likely the package or your host. Clean up "
"with ``rm -rf test_venv``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:287
msgid "Files not in the documented locations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:289
msgid ""
"pipx after 1.16.0 places ``PIPX_HOME`` and the data, cache, and log "
"directories in the platform locations `platformdirs <https://pypi.org/"
"project/platformdirs/>`_ reports. Earlier versions defaulted ``PIPX_HOME`` "
"to ``~/.local/pipx`` (or ``~/pipx`` on Windows), and pipx keeps using such a "
"directory when it exists. The venv cache and logs still move to the platform "
"cache and log directories even when pipx falls back to an older home, "
"because both are disposable. Setting ``PIPX_HOME`` yourself keeps them "
"inside it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:295
msgid ""
"For the full old-to-new path map and how to migrate, see :ref:`platformdirs-"
"migration` and :doc:`move-installation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:299
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/troubleshoot.rst:305
msgid ""
"A clean ``pipx health`` (exit status 0) confirms every managed environment "
"can run its interpreter."
msgstr ""
